       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient could develop serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity (QT prolongation). It's probably a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. As CEO, you'd normally not be the one placing this order.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- If the prescriber meant a standard dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it.\n- If a clinician really does intend 1000 mg, they should confirm it directly with pharmacy and the ordering team. They should also add a note with the clinical rationale.\n\nWhich dose do you want entered?"
